  "description": "RS-CapRet is a Vision and Language foundational model for remote sensing, capable of image captioning and text-image retrieval. It combines a frozen large language model (LLamaV2-7B) with a CLIP-based vision encoder finetuned on remote sensing image captioning datasets, using trainable linear layers to bridge modalities. The model achieves state-of-the-art or competitive results on several remote sensing benchmarks.",
  "sci:doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2402.06475",
  "license": null,
  "assets": null,
  "mlm:architecture": "CLIP ViT-L/14 (vision encoder), LLamaV2-7B (language model)",
  "mlm:total_parameters": null,
  "pretext_training_type": "Contrastive language-image pre-training; cross-entropy for captioning",
  "masking_strategy": null,
  "pretraining": "CLIP vision encoder is finetuned on an aggregation of remote sensing image captioning datasets (Cap-4). The language model (LLamaV2-7B) is kept frozen. Only linear projection layers and [RET] token embedding are trained.",
